# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by default.
#
# This repository is public and holds a household's real recipes, on purpose.
# What it must not carry is other people's details — the names of relatives and
# friends, contact details, addresses — and anything the household would rather
# keep, which goes under private/. See SECURITY.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real recipes, and anything else that is nobody else's business. Git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so nothing below this can be re-included.
/private/

# The scanner's literal denylist is itself a personal-data file, and the salt
# that keys its digests is what keeps tools/denylist.hashes inert in public.
tools/denylist.txt
tools/denylist.salt

# Photographs. A picture of a dish on a kitchen table shows the kitchen.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.heif
*.webp
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp
*.pdf

# Exports and scrapes from recipe apps, which arrive full of personal notes.
# Note the breadth of *.json: the Markdown linter's config is therefore called
# .pymarkdown, with no extension, so that it stays tracked. There are no
# re-inclusions in this file and CI fails if one appears.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.paprikarecipes
*.paprikarecipe
*.mxp
*.mx2

# Ordinary noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
